  "summary": "Knoxville Police Department's Flock license plate reader cameras were switched off Jan. 1, 2026 after the city's contract with Flock expired and a short-term extension could not be reached. KPD is transitioning to a new vendor, Axon, but new cameras aren't expected to be operational until mid-2026, which attorneys warn could hinder investigations.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The city's previous vendor, Flock, shut off the cameras Jan. 1 after its contract expired.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    },
    {
      "quote": "Knoxville police confirmed they attempted to secure a short-term contract extension with Flock before the agreement expired, but no deal was reached.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock turned KPD cameras off Jan. 1 without notifying the department, a KPD spokesman said.",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    }
